{"metadata":{"title":"Capabilities","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"OpenUSD"}],"role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OpenUSD in Swift is currently evolving and may change in the future. Here are some key features currently supported:","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Reference-types-in-Swift","text":"Reference types in Swift","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UsdStage and SdfLayer are imported as classes in Swift and behave like classes written in Swift. When Swift passes a raw pointer to UsdStage or SdfLayer, Swift automatically increments or decrements the underlying reference count as needed, allowing Swift or C++ to influence the lifetime of the same UsdStage or SdfLayer."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func makeTempStage() -> pxr.UsdStage {","    return Overlay.Dereference(pxr.UsdStage.CreateNew(\"\/tmp\/myStage.usda\", .LoadAll))","}","","func defineXform(_ stage: pxr.UsdStage, _ path: pxr.SdfPath) {","    stage.DefinePrim(path, .UsdGeomTokens.Xform)","}","","let stage = makeTempStage()","defineXform(stage, \"\/hello\")","let layer = Overlay.Dereference(stage.GetRootLayer())","layer.Save(false)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/WhatIsAForeignReferenceType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/ForeignReferenceTypesAndSmartPointers","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for more information."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When working in Swift, do not use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfRefPtr.pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfWeakPtr.pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" to dereference Pixar’s smart pointers, as the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" property is unsafe. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Overlay.Dereference(_:TfRefPtr)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Overlay.Dereference(_:TfWeakPtr)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Warning","style":"warning"},{"anchor":"Swift-protocol-conformances","text":"Swift protocol conformances","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Many OpenUSD types conform to one or more of the following protocols:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ExpressibleByStringLiteral","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExpressibleByArrayLiteral"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sequence","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let token: pxr.TfToken = \"my custom token\" \/\/ TfToken conforms to ExpressibleByStringLiteral","var prims: Set<pxr.UsdPrim> = Set<pxr.UsdPrim>() \/\/ UsdPrim conforms to Hashable","let numbers: pxr.VtIntArray = [1, 2, 3] \/\/ VtIntArray conforms to ExpressibleByArrayLiteral"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"TfNotice-support","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"TfNotice support"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift code can register for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfNotice"},{"type":"text","text":" callbacks by using "},{"overridingTitle":"pxr.TfNotice.Register","type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"pxr.TfNotice.Register","type":"codeVoice"}],"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD\/C++\/pxr\/TfNotice\/Register(_:_:)-28red"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["class StageWatcher {","    var stage: pxr.UsdStage","    var key: pxr.TfNotice.SwiftKey","","    init(stage: pxr.UsdStage) {","        self.stage = stage","","        key = pxr.TfNotice.Register(stage, pxr.UsdNotice.ObjectsChanged.self) { notice in","            print(\"Resynced: \\(notice.GetResyncedPaths())\")","            print(\"Changed info only: \\(notice.GetChangedInfoOnlyPaths())\")","        }","    }","    deinit {","        pxr.TfNotice.Revoke(key)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more information, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/WorkingWithTfNotice","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"More-details","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"More details"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For details about supported features, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/DifferencesInSwift","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Learn about the current capabilities of OpenUSD in Swift","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD"]]},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/Capabilities","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/DifferencesInSwift","doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/CurrentLimitations"],